# From the repository root: cp apps/api/.env.example apps/api/.env
NODE_ENV=development

# Required: local PostgreSQL inside WSL, using a dedicated non-superuser role.
# Replace the password below; URL-encode special characters in passwords.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://lumo:replace-with-local-password@localhost:5432/lumo

# Required for integration/E2E tests: use a separate database ending in _test.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://lumo:replace-with-local-password@localhost:5432/lumo_test

# Required: paste a unique secret generated with: openssl rand -hex 48
# Must contain at least 32 characters. Never commit your populated .env file.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# Exact origins only: no paths or trailing slashes.
API_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3001
WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
PORT=3001
HOST=127.0.0.1
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Development/test emails are written here (relative to apps/api); never served by HTTP.
# These environments always use files, even when a Resend key is present.
MAIL_DIR=../../.local/mail
EMAIL_FROM=hello@lumolynk.com
EMAIL_FROM_NAME=Lumo

# Production: NODE_ENV=production, HTTPS origins, and a Resend API key are required.
# EMAIL_FROM must use lumolynk.com or a subdomain verified for sending, e.g. noreply@notify.lumolynk.com.
# There is no file fallback.
# Keep this key server-only; do not prefix it with VITE_ or put it in web/desktop env files.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# Use HOST=0.0.0.0 when listening inside a container. Setup: docs/email.md

# Optional until Meetings is used; missing configuration fails closed.
# The App ID is public. The certificate must stay on the API server.
# Use `agora project env write apps/api/.env --append --project Lumo` from the root
# to configure existing authorized credentials without printing them.
# AGORA_APP_ID=74840af2ab78410fbeb9e5de554b6689
# AGORA_APP_CERTIFICATE=
# Quote App Keys: an unquoted # starts a dotenv comment.

# Storage is shared by Drive, avatars, Messenger, HR files and Office revisions.
# Provider defaults to aws. Leave all bucket settings unset to disable storage.
# STORAGE_PROVIDER=aws
# AWS S3: use the SDK default credential chain (IAM role in production, AWS_PROFILE for local SSO).
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# AWS_S3_BUCKET=your-private-drive-bucket
# Optional local credentials only; never copy these into web/desktop environment files.
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=
# DigitalOcean Spaces alternative (replace the AWS configuration above):
# STORAGE_PROVIDER=digitalocean
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# AWS_S3_BUCKET=your-private-space
# S3_ENDPOINT=https://nyc3.digitaloceanspaces.com
# A bucket origin is also accepted when it matches AWS_S3_BUCKET, e.g.
# AWS_S3_BUCKET=lumo-prod with S3_ENDPOINT=https://lumo-prod.sgp1.digitaloceanspaces.com.
# It is normalized to https://sgp1.digitaloceanspaces.com before configuring the SDK.
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your-spaces-access-key
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your-spaces-secret-key
# AWS_REGION is the SDK signing region; the Spaces location comes from S3_ENDPOINT.
# Keep the legacy AWS_REGION/AWS_S3_BUCKET names for both providers.
# Dedicated S3 credentials override the AWS chain and do not inherit AWS_SESSION_TOKEN.
# Optional for either provider; false uses virtual-hosted bucket URLs (Spaces default).
# S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=false
# For AWS, leave S3_ENDPOINT and dedicated S3 credentials unset to retain SDK defaults.
# DRIVE_MAX_FILE_BYTES=1073741824
# Comma-separated exact MIME types, type/*, or * (default).
# DRIVE_ALLOWED_MIME_TYPES=*
# Bucket CORS, least-privilege IAM and lifecycle configuration: docs/drive-storage.md

# ONLYOFFICE Docs Cloud for Docs, Sheets and Slides (Wiki uses CodeMirror + Yjs).
# Configure all three settings together. Keep the tenant secret on this server only.
# Find the Document Server address and secret in https://docscloud.onlyoffice.com/.
# Exact HTTPS origins: no paths, query strings or trailing slashes.
# ONLYOFFICE_DOCUMENT_SERVER_URL=https://your-document-server.example.com
# ONLYOFFICE_JWT_SECRET=
# Public HTTPS ingress/tunnel forwarding to this API, reachable by Docs Cloud.
# ONLYOFFICE_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://your-api-tunnel.example.com
# ONLYOFFICE_MODE=cloud
# For a self-hosted Docs instance, use self-hosted and the same HTTPS/API contracts.
# Reuse AWS_REGION/AWS_S3_BUCKET above; there is no separate Office storage.
# Setup status and preflight requirements: docs/onlyoffice-implementation-notes.md

# Maximum avatar upload size in bytes (up to 5 MiB).
AVATAR_MAX_BYTES=5242880
